# pylock.android.toml is intentionally TRACKED here — this is an on-device
# gate example: CI's android_emulator job runs its contract smoke test on an
# API 24 emulator (min_sdk), and its lock records the exact wheel hashes that
# passed there and on the Pixel 8a. Regenerating it would detach that result
# from the binaries it was obtained from, and would make
# `kivyforge lock -p android --check` unable to fail. See "Example-repo lock
# policy" in docs/design/common/03-lockfile-concept.md.
